<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <title><%= content_for(:title) || "Lineup" %></title>
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=1200">
  <%# Montserrat is SERVED SAME-ORIGIN from studio-engine's vendored woff2
      (studio/montserrat-latin.woff2 + -latin-ext), through the asset pipeline. No CDN.
      This layout does not render studio/_head, which is why the engine's own vendoring
      (0.56.4) did not reach it and this file kept its Google Fonts link after every
      other surface had lost one.

      WHY IT MATTERED HERE MORE THAN ELSEWHERE. A Google Fonts stylesheet blocks the
      load event; the font FILES it names do not. So the page went interactive in the
      fallback face and every glyph was re-measured when Montserrat landed. On the
      board that cost swallowed clicks. This page is a CAPTURE SURFACE — script/
      capture_lineup.js drives it with CDP and records a screencast — so a late
      re-measure does not merely annoy, it reflows text inside a video after the
      composition is judged done.

      WHY font-display: block, WHERE THE ENGINE USES optional. They are answering
      different questions and the difference is deliberate. `optional` gives no swap
      period at all, which is right for an interactive page: the font either arrives
      inside a ~100ms block window or that page-load simply uses the fallback, and
      nothing ever reflows. On a capture surface that failure mode is the WORST one
      available — the recording would silently ship in system-ui, branded wrong, with
      nothing red anywhere to say so. `block` cannot do that: it waits, then paints
      the real face. The wait costs this page nothing, because the capture already
      holds for `networkidle` and then for body[data-images-ready='true'] before it
      records a single frame, so the block window closes long before capture starts.
      A human previewing the page pays at most a brief FOIT on a same-origin,
      preloaded file.

      The weight axis is 100..900 because the vendored file is a VARIABLE font — one
      file carries every weight this layout asks for (400/600/700/800/900). %>
  <link rel="preload" href="<%= asset_path("studio/montserrat-latin.woff2") %>" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
  <style>
    @font-face {
      font-family: 'Montserrat';
      font-style: normal;
      font-weight: 100 900;
      font-display: block;
      src: url('<%= asset_path("studio/montserrat-latin.woff2") %>') format('woff2');
      unicode-range: U+0000-00FF, U+0131, U+0152-0153, U+02BB-02BC, U+02C6, U+02DA, U+02DC, U+0304, U+0308, U+0329, U+2000-206F, U+20AC, U+2122, U+2191, U+2193, U+2212, U+2215, U+FEFF, U+FFFD;
    }
    @font-face {
      font-family: 'Montserrat';
      font-style: normal;
      font-weight: 100 900;
      font-display: block;
      src: url('<%= asset_path("studio/montserrat-latin-ext.woff2") %>') format('woff2');
      unicode-range: U+0100-02BA, U+02BD-02C5, U+02C7-02CC, U+02CE-02D7, U+02DD-02FF, U+0304, U+0308, U+0329, U+1D00-1DBF, U+1E00-1E9F, U+1EF2-1EFF, U+2020, U+20A0-20AB, U+20AD-20C0, U+2113, U+2C60-2C7F, U+A720-A7FF;
    }
  </style>
  <style>
    *, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }
    html, body { margin: 0; padding: 0; background: #0b0b14; }
    body { font-family: "Montserrat", system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif; }
    img { display: block; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <%= yield %>
</body>
</html>
